Entry Level Sales Representative (Outside Sales)

1.&nbsp; Conducts department billing compliance audits by comparing medical record against patient account. &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
2.&nbsp; Perform patient account research to prevent billing errors in response to questions from various departments throughout the hospital.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
3.&nbsp; Prepare for and conduct audits requested by governmental and managed care payors, comparing medical record against patient account to ensure complete and accurate charge capture.&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
4.&nbsp;&nbsp; Assists in the development of compliance audit standards. &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
5.&nbsp; Performs training based on results of department quarterly audits and audits of charge capture activities.
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
6.&nbsp; Prepare written reports, recommendations and corrective action plans based on audits for operation, strategic and policy changes as the result of audits.

Position Summary:&nbsp;
The Registered Nurse provides professional nursing care in community and in home settings. The registered nurse utilizes Comprehensive Nursing Assessments which identify the child&rsquo;s and/or family members&rsquo; physical, emotional and behavioral needs and which are developmentally appropriate. This position requires on call availability to provide crisis stabilization and intervention; local travel and flexibility to work a non-traditional schedule in a high-demand work situation.&nbsp;
The Registered Nurse demonstrates the ability to carry out nursing interventions and evaluations that are age appropriate and therapeutically sound.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Essential Responsibilities&nbsp;&nbsp;
Service Delivery&nbsp;
1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Functions as the primary health educator to children and families for screening and consultation regarding issues of diet, weight loss, smoke cessation, sleep, hygiene, sexuality and general health and wellness.&nbsp;
2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Functions as liaison with non Pressley Ridge health care providers, including primary care, specialists, and mental health providers.&nbsp;
3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Provides nursing care based on needs of the youth / family member.&nbsp;
4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Conducts nursing assessment on intake and documents.&nbsp;
5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Assists the family and HELP Team to integrate the physical health information into the treatment plan and evaluate progress.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Regulatory Compliance&nbsp;
1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Updates skills and maintain necessary credential(s).&nbsp;
2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Demonstrates knowledge of proper documentation and charting procedures and completes in a timely manner.&nbsp;
3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Adheres to all best practice standards as relates to accreditation and licensing.&nbsp;
4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Follows all Pressley Ridge policies, procedures and protocols.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Quality Improvement&nbsp;
1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Utilizes data for decision making and performance improvement from the following sources: Environmental Site Safety committees; Client/Caregiver Survey; Stakeholder Survey; Client Record Reviews; Root Cause Analysis; Gap Analysis Training Transcripts; Interagency Meetings.&nbsp;
2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Participates and monitors program adherence to trauma sensitive, coercion free model indicators.&nbsp;
3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Participates in System of Care meetings.
&nbsp;&nbsp;

DENISON UNIVERSITY LIBRARY


LIBRARY ASSOCIATE I


Part-time, 25.5 hrs/week
&nbsp;
Denison University Library is seeking a part-time Library Associate I to perform a variety of library duties requiring judgment in the application of policies and procedures within the area of assignment, involving use of library's automation system, various software packages, conventional library materials and media equipment, printers, copiers and scanners. Provide initial screening for library users having problems with library computer equipment and software programs provided on public work stations.
&nbsp;

Retail Sales &ndash; Management Opportunity!
&nbsp;&nbsp;
Furnishing You With Opportunity.
&nbsp;&nbsp;
Are you a highly motivated individual ready for a career change? Are you ready for an opportunity to grow, learn and develop professionally? Join our team at Sofa Mart &amp; Oak Express Company! We are currently seeking highly motivated individuals from all kinds of backgrounds to take advantage of our Entry Level Management Training Program. With over 35 years of success in the bedding industry, we equip professionals from a variety of backgrounds with the knowledge and expertise to become successful Retail Sales Managers.
&nbsp;&nbsp;
Like our products, careers at Sofa Mart &amp; Oak Express are built to last. Our strong industry position creates a stable workplace where you can feel secure in your success.
&nbsp;&nbsp;
Our successful Retail Managers have come from a variety of backgrounds in multiple industries including marketing, automotive, customer service, hospitality, industrial, administration, healthcare, insurance, human resources and medical care. We are a unique leader in the furniture industry, and we love our Associates and Managers who are diverse and have a unique variety of experience! Take a career leap, apply today!
&nbsp;&nbsp;

Entry Level Retail Sales Manager &ndash; Management Trainee &ndash; Retail Store Training &ndash; Entry Level &ndash; Customer Service &ndash; Hospitality &ndash; Administration

&nbsp;&nbsp;
Benefits
As an Entry Level Retail Sales Manager Trainee, we recognize your drive and ambition, and we want to help you advance on your desired career path. With us, you will have access to the training and resources you need to thrive at your new career. Sofa Mart &amp; Oak Express gives you the keys to succeed as a Retail Sales Manager!
&nbsp;&nbsp;
We recognize that you dedicate time and effort to your job, and we want you to have the resources to keep achieving. Here are some of the benefits our Trainees enjoy!
&nbsp;&nbsp;

    Competitive Pay plus commission
    Medical and Dental benefits
    Paid Vacation
    401(k) retirement savings plan
    Additional cash rewards

&nbsp;&nbsp;

Entry Level Retail Sales Manager &ndash; Entry Level Trainee &ndash; Customer Service &ndash; Hospitality &ndash; Administration

&nbsp;&nbsp;
Job Responsibilities
As an Entry Level Retail Sales Manager Trainee, you will be selling our unique array of furniture and accessories. You will receive hands on training in sales, marketing and business development techniques. You will shadow Store Managers, learning all of the aspects of retail and people management. Our program hinges on understanding, mastering and being able to lead your own team successfully.
&nbsp;&nbsp;
Other responsibilities of the Management Trainee position include:

    Greeting and assisting customers ascertaining their wants and needs
    Answering customer questions and inquiries regarding products and services
    Seeking out information and knowledge regarding new products
    Setting and achieving personal goals
    Presenting pricing, preparing contracts and processing transactions in POS
    Placing orders and locating stock
    Maintaining knowledge of current promotions and policies regarding payment, exchanges and store security
    Participating in merchandising and product displays

&nbsp; &nbsp;

Entry Level Retail Sales Manager &ndash; Entry Level Trainee &ndash; Customer Service &ndash; Hospitality &ndash; Administration

