Job is located in Lansing, MI.JOB DESCRIPTION
Primary Care Physician
Full Time - Days

Our growth is YOUR opportunity to make a difference in the lives of the frail and elderly - join our program start up in Lansing, MI.

About us:
Since 1896, Volunteers of America has been dedicated to "reaching and uplifting" the American people. Now in our second century of service, Volunteers of America is one of the nation's largest and most comprehensive human services organizations touching the lives of more than 2 million each year. We are opening an exciting new PACE program in Lansing. Michigan.

The Program of All-Inclusive Care for the Elderly (PACE&reg;) model is centered on the belief that it is better for the well-being of seniors with chronic care needs and their families to be served in the community whenever possible. Delivering all needed medical and supportive services, a PACE program is able to provide the entire continuum of care and services to seniors with chronic care needs while maintaining their independence in their home for as long as possible.&nbsp;

Services include the following:

    adult day care that offers nursing; physical, occupational and recreational therapies; meals; nutritional counseling; social work and personal care;
    medical care provided by a PACE physician familiar with the history, needs and preferences of each participant;
    home health care and personal care;
    all necessary prescription drugs;
    social services;
    medical specialties, such as audiology, dentistry, optometry, podiatry and speech therapy;
    respite care; and
    hospital and nursing home care when necessary.

If you have a passion for the elderly and would like to be apart of this new service in Lansing, apply today!

