The Physical therapist organizes and carries out physical therapy programs in the hospital for inpatients or outpatients, to facilitate the rehabilitation of the mentally or physically handicapped.&nbsp;&nbsp;

The staff&nbsp; PT provides direct patient focused care to include physical therapy evaluations and quality treatment with short and long term goals determined by the patient&rsquo;s needs.&nbsp;

The staff&nbsp; PT may work with any /all patients of the following age groups based upon individual responsibility, training, and competency:&nbsp; Infants (age 0-18 months), Children (age 19 months-12 years), Adolescents (age 13 years &ndash;17 years), Adults (age 18 years &ndash; 64 years), and Geriatrics (age 65+ years).


Essential Functions:
1) Demonstrate and articulate sound clinical reasoning in synthesizing complex evaluation data, identifying diagnosis, and developing a comprehensive plan of care

2) Develop and update an appropriate plan of care in collaboration with the patient/family; related to their age and lifestyle with measurable long and short term goals

3) Utilize appropriate methods and materials for effective learning, monitoring the response to education, and adapting the program appropriately&nbsp;
&nbsp;
4) Initiate patient and family education in a timely manner relative to age, readiness to learn, and emotional status


