Summary:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Responsible for assisting consumers in acquiring, retaining and improving communication, socialization, self-direction, self-help and adaptive skills necessary to reside in the community.&nbsp; The Community Inclusion staff facilitates&nbsp;the consumer&rsquo;s social interaction; use of natural supports and typical community services available to all people; and participation in education and volunteer activities.
&nbsp;&nbsp;
Responsibilities:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

    As directed within the Individual Support Plan (ISP), provide supports to achieve identified outcomes.
    If the consumer receives Behavioral Specialist Services (BSS), the Community Inclusion staff will implement the Behavior Support Plan (BSP) as outlined and, if necessary, the crisis intervention plan.
    As directed within the ISP, provide on-site modeling of behavior, behavior support, intensive behavioral episode intervention, training, cueing and/or supervision.&nbsp;
    As determined necessary, the Community Inclusion staff may provide the consumer with personal assistance in completing activities of daily living and instrumental activities of daily living (with the intent of this service being the reduction of the level of personal assistance).
    As directed within the ISP and BSP, collect and record data regarding consumer progress toward identified outcomes as documented to be utilized when reviewing the ISP and BSP.&nbsp;&nbsp;
    As directed within the ISP, provide specific supports to assist the consumer in developing daily living skills and social and cultural interaction skills with his or her peer group, family, and other social groups or settings
    The Community Inclusion staff will provide services in the consumer&rsquo;s home and/or at other community locations as determined appropriate to assist in achievement of identified outcomes. &nbsp;
    The Community Inclusion staff will transport the consumer to identified community locations.
    As directed within the ISP, provide assistance in providing individualized, supervised recreational and cultural opportunities.
    At all times offer honest, respectful, and caring relationships to the consumer and his/her family.
    The Community Inclusion staff will maintain an assigned planned schedule by the Administrative Supervisor that guides the use of authorized time with the consumer.
    The Community Inclusion staff will collaborate with other members of the ISP team and other professionals working in the home or other community settings and will be present and participate in any meetings, supervision and trainings as required.
    All other reasonable and necessary program specific activities at the discretion and direction of the Program Supervisors.

