Certified Occupational Therapy Assistant ( COTA )

Job Responsibilities
As a Certified Occupational Therapist Assistant, you will help injured workers re-enter the labor force and teach them how to compensate for lost motor skills. You will also help individuals with learning disabilities increase their independence through therapy activities that fit their needs and capabilities. Another essential aspect of a Certified Occupational Therapist Assistant&rsquo;s work is to observe and record patients&rsquo; progress, attitudes and behavior, and maintain this information in client records.&nbsp;

Additional responsibilities include:

    Monitoring patients&rsquo; performance in therapy activities and providing encouragement
    Instructing or assisting in the instruction of patients and families in home programs, basic living skills and the care and use of adaptive equipment&nbsp;
    Implementing or assisting occupational therapists with the implementation of treatment plans&nbsp;
    Evaluating the daily living skills and capacities of physically, developmentally or emotionally disabled patients
    Aiding patients in dressing and grooming themselves
    Reporting to supervisors, verbally or in writing, on patients&rsquo; progress, attitudes and behavior&nbsp;
    Communicating and collaborating with other health care professionals involved with the care of a patient
    Maintaining and promoting a positive attitude toward clients and their treatment programs
    Must be bi-lingual in both English and Spanish&nbsp;



