SOUTHERN ILLINOIS LIVING CENTER


d.b.a Clinton Manor Living Center
&nbsp;
Our Mission here at Clinton Manor Living is to:
&bull;Empower staff to invite change and recognize differences
&bull;Encourage people to live as they choose with integrity, dignity, and quality of life
&bull;Enhance opportunities for people to develop and maintain their personal connections
&nbsp;
Job Title:  Direct Support Professional&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Reports to:  Family Program Supervisor/QIDP

Provide and ensure all necessary supports and service are being provided to individuals with developmental disabilities who reside in the facility in order for them to live as fully and independently as possible.  Assure completion of all tasks and assignments as required by state regulations and agency policy and procedures.
&nbsp;
Essential Duties and Responsibilities
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Assists and provides all essential supports to each individual to the least degree necessary enabling the individual to acquire and maintain skills that foster independence.
&nbsp;
&nbsp;Assist and train individuals to complete everyday living skills such as proper bathing, personal hygiene, good oral hygiene, grooming (clothes, nails, hair, shaving, hand washing).

&nbsp;
Promote and Advocate for individuals to live with integrity, dignity and freedom of choice; therefore enhancing their quality of life and ensuring the individual&rsquo;s rights at all times.

&nbsp;
Enhance community inclusion by utilizing community-based resources to achieve maximum integration and independence for the individuals.

&nbsp;Assist with the implementation of the Individuals Service Plan (ISP) and respond to individual behaviors according to their specific behavior management plans.

&nbsp;Ensure all residents are monitored/supervised at all times and the environment is free from safety hazards.  Assure that designated areas are locked.  Report any unsafe act or unsafe equipment immediately to supervisor.

&nbsp;Ensures all outlined unusual incidents/injuries are responded to and communicated to Administration who is listed on the Emergency Chain of Command.

&nbsp;Arranges and provides transportation of individuals to and from their designated sites for medical, social or any other need of transportation.

&nbsp;Follows all procedures for implementation and documentation for each resident&rsquo;s goals or programs; works with the team to develop, implement and monitor the processes for their goals.

&nbsp;Handles individual&rsquo;s personal funds and company funds according to established procedures including the proper documentation of all expenditures.
&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;Follows established procedures in maintaining the integrity of records including the withholding of information, both written and verbal, from persons not authorized to receive it.

&nbsp;Maintains promptness and reliability of work attendance.  Clocks in and out correctly.

&nbsp;Ensure living areas and environment is clean and disinfected properly.  Properly care for resident&rsquo;s property, clothing and shows respect for their personal property.
&nbsp;
Maintain wheelchairs and all adaptive equipment as properly instructed.

&nbsp;
Report any observation or suspicion of abuse or neglect to the Administrator of the facility immediately.
&nbsp;
&nbsp;Operations Functions (Non-Essential)
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Complies with all agency policies and procedures.
&nbsp;&nbsp;
Provides a model of promptness, cooperation, caring, independence, teamwork and problem solving for individuals and situations at all times.
&nbsp;&nbsp;
Assists in obtaining all eligible financial resources for individuals served.
&nbsp;&nbsp;
Direct visitors to the proper Personnel for assistance. 
&nbsp;&nbsp;
Participate in licensure surveys and accreditation process.
&nbsp;&nbsp;
Staff Development
&nbsp;
Attend and participate in DSP required State of Illinois training within 120 days of hire (if applicable).
&nbsp;
&nbsp;Coordinate with all co-workers and supervisors as needed to provide total individualized care for each resident.
&nbsp;
Attend and participate in annual OSHA and CDC in-service training programs for hazard communication, TB management, and bloodborne pathogens and HIPPA standards.
&nbsp;
&nbsp;Create and maintain an atmosphere of warmth, personal interest, and positive emphasis, as well as a calm environment throughout the Agency.
&nbsp;
&nbsp;Attends and completes all training requirements set forth by the agency and attends all scheduled training sessions.
&nbsp;
&nbsp;Safety and Sanitation
&nbsp;
