JOB TITLE: Showroom Specialist

&nbsp;

&nbsp;
Position Summary:&nbsp;
This position is a Sales Support role, assisting outside sales reps to
generate leads, schedule appointments, make confirmation calls, follow-up with
customers, generate and process orders, and perform clerical duties as
necessary.&nbsp; Position is part time,
afternoons from 2PM to 6PM and every other Saturday from 9AM to 1PM.&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES include the following:&nbsp; 
&nbsp;
Uses computer
driven scheduling system to schedule in-home consultations with prospective
customers.
&nbsp;
Describes and
demonstrates product in the showroom using samples or catalogs, emphasizing
features and benefits of&nbsp;products. 
&nbsp;
Administers,
verifies and submits accurate product orders to appropriate Material
Coordinator and/or Corporation by communicating with Sales
Representative(s) and customers, and having solid knowledge of products,
systems, and procedures.
&nbsp;
Learns and
uses the&nbsp;Direct Quoting system&nbsp; in conjunction with other systems to
enter orders, providing complete and accurate information to ensure the correct
product is ordered, built, and delivered to the customer.
&nbsp;
Maintains
product displays in working order, and calls for service when displays need
repairs.
&nbsp;
Assists
Outside Sales Representative(s) in generating leads and prospecting new
business, as well as following-up on leads and outstanding&nbsp;proposals.
&nbsp;
Organizes and
orders product literature to maintain appropriate quantities for use by outside
sales reps and customers.
&nbsp;
Manages leads
by gathering and preserving accurate customer information and entering into the
lead management database.
&nbsp;
Answers and
directs customer inquiries (in person, via the Internet or email or via the
phone) by asking leading questions and pre-qualifying.
&nbsp;
Prepares
activity reports using required systems and software as needed by management.
&nbsp;
Maintains the
appearance of the&nbsp;Showroom by performing basic cleaning duties such as
vacuuming, emptying trash, and cleaning product displays.
&nbsp;
Meets company
safety requirements by keeping work area neat and clean, following all company
safety policies and procedures, and reporting any safety concerns 
