ABOUT OUR COMPANY
&nbsp;
Ernest Health owns and operates community-based acute rehabilitation and long-term acute care facilities in Arizona, Colorado, Idaho, Indiana, Montana, New Mexico, South Carolina, Texas, Utah and Wyoming. We are dedicated to providing high quality, cost-effective physical medicine and rehabilitation services to promote the recovery of individuals who have functional deficits resulting from injury or illness as well as those with chronic or complex medical conditions. We promote a healing and nurturing environment at each of our facilities, responding to the medical, physical, psychological and social needs of our patients.
&nbsp;
ABOUT OUR HOSPITAL
&nbsp;
Our Northern Colorado Rehabilitation Facility, designed solely for the provision of specialized rehabilitative care, is the only freestanding acute rehabilitation hospital serving northern Colorado. Since opening its doors in 2005, our hospital has been rated in the top 10% of all inpatient rehab facilities in the United Stated for 8 consecutive years! Through our inpatient and outpatient rehabilitation programs, we are able to utilize our unique design and responsive environment to help patients recover quickly and return home with a renewed sense of self-sufficiency.
&nbsp;
ABOUT OUR SEARCH
&nbsp;
Northern Colorado Rehabilitation Hospital (NCRH) is currently seeking an experienced Physical Therapist. Make a direct difference today by joining our team of dedicated professionals working together to attain a common goal &ndash; giving the gift of time through great patient care. Competitive wages and benefits await you! 
&nbsp;
BASIC PURPOSE OF THE JOB
&nbsp;
The Physical Therapist evaluates a patient&rsquo;s physical and functional capacities and plans, organizes, coordinates, and administers goal-directed, activity oriented treatment while exercising professional judgment, knowledge, and skills in managing treatment plans for the purpose of promoting/restoring optimum independence in daily life tasks and physical functions. The Physical Therapist ensures continuation of performance through effective education of the patient, family, support system, and home program, if applicable.&nbsp; These functions are carried out according to hospital policy and in accordance with the mission and vision of the hospital and consistent with the philosophy of the department.&nbsp; The Physical Therapist supervises/provides physical therapy services to patients ranging in age from 14 to 100+ in an inpatient and/or outpatient environment.&nbsp; The Physical Therapist supervises supportive personnel and actively participates in departmental activities and processes.

